  "title": "Site Reliability Engineer (SRE)",
  "summary": "A site reliability engineer keeps production services fast and available, using software engineering to run operations. They sit in a platform or infrastructure team, set reliability targets called SLOs (service level objectives) and take part in on-call.",
  "dailyDuties": [
    "Set SLOs and error budgets and act on them",
    "Instrument services with logs, metrics and traces",
    "Take on-call shifts and write blameless postmortems",
